[SIZE="4"][B]Inventory Companion Changelog[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.8.1[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]The tracker, currency panel, and resource bars now show only on Inventory Companion's own settings page, not elsewhere in the keyboard settings menu. They leave a little more room beside the settings page without reserving space for a header or footer.
[*]HUD panels make room for the equipment, stats, and header in keyboard inventory, and clear the visible edge of the right-hand backdrop in inventory, banks, the furniture vault, merchants, and fences. Automatic moves do not overwrite saved positions.
[*]HUD panels keep clear of ESO's bottom keybind bar and its background in supported keyboard screens. When there's room directly above the footer, progress bars move up without shifting sideways.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.8.0[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Withdraw one item or all but one from the Craft Bag or Furniture Vault. For stacks over 201, withdraw one 200-item stack or move all but one in batches of up to 200.
[*]Stow one item, all but one, or the entire backpack stack in the Craft Bag without entering a quantity. Thanks Delena!
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.7.2[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE="2"][B]Your panels stay visible and make room for ESO windows[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Keep your tracker, currency panel, and resource bars in view while using keyboard inventory, banks (both deposit and withdrawal), the furniture vault, merchants, fences, Inventory Companion editors, and settings. Only panels that normally show stay visible.
[*]Panels already clear of ESO windows stay put. If a window opens or grows into their space, affected panels stack to the right when possible, then try the left. In tight spaces, Inventory Companion panels may overlap.
[*]The addon stops checking panel visibility when no panel or settings preview needs it.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]Snap panels into place and save a layout for each screen[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Drop a panel near another to line up their edges or dock them together. Drop it on top of another panel and it can snap to the nearest clear side. Hold [B]Shift[/B] as you release to keep exactly where you dropped it.
[*]Put your bars beside the bank and your tracker somewhere different in inventory. Each character keeps their own positions for each screen, even on a shared profile. Positions survive logout, closing the screen restores your normal layout, and automatic moves never overwrite your saved positions.
[*]Resetting a panel's position also clears its saved screen positions. [B]Copy Full Profile[/B] includes them.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]Choose how wide your currency panel is[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Open [B]Currency Summary Panel[/B] settings and try the new [B]Grid Columns[/B] slider. Use fewer columns for a narrow panel or more for a shorter, wider one. The preview updates immediately without changing your resource order or formatting.
[*]Your active profile remembers the choice. The maximum depends on available resources, and [B]Reset Panel[/B] returns the grid to three columns without resetting positions.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]Smaller tracking updates[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Treasure Maps now matches names without requiring a space after "Treasure Map".
[*]Existing custom groups that exactly match a built-in group name can carry their patterns, display preferences, and AutoCategory placements over to the built-in group.
[*]Added an optional Furniture Materials group for Mundane Rune, Heartwood, Regulus, Bast, Clean Pelt, Alchemical Resin, Decorative Wax, and Ochre. It starts hidden, with notifications off.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]Saved settings upgrade[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Saved-variable schema 11 keeps panel preferences and layouts with their profiles. Keep a backup before updating if you may want to return to a previous version; older builds cannot use the upgraded settings.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.6.3[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Guild-bank right-click actions now deposit or withdraw one item, or all but one. Partial deposits require guild-bank deposit access. Partial withdrawals temporarily withdraw the whole stack and return the remainder, require both deposit and withdrawal access, and can be disabled with the account-wide setting (on by default).
[*]New optional AutoCategory integration lets you manage native categories alongside Inventory Companion groups. Set independent Display and Priority orders for Backpack, Bank, Guild Bank, House Bank, Crafting Station, Craft Bag and Furniture Vault. AutoCategory remains responsible for classifying and displaying inventory items.
[*]Use Hide and Show to exclude or include categories in one inventory area without deleting their definitions or changing other areas. Move the special Other heading in Display order without changing its catch-all matching behavior. Reorder selections and copy both orders between areas.
[*]Account-wide and character-specific profiles now include panel preferences and positions, editor filters, tracking configuration and AutoCategory layouts. First-time character setup copies the account profile; later switches resume that character's retained settings. Copy From in Main Settings replaces a complete profile after confirmation.
[*]Integration enablement, item transfer delay, chest-stack merging and diagnostic controls remain account-wide. AutoCategory integration is off by default and has a guided first setup and a dedicated recovery panel.
[*]Streamlined Main Settings and consistent editor navigation bring Manage Tracking, Manage Groups and Manage AutoCategory together. Tracking has aligned single-line Show and Notify summaries, Groups has name filtering, and all three editors offer visit-scoped Undo changes.
[*]Group patterns now support Include and Exclude rules: an item must match an Include and no Exclude in that group. Per-item and per-group backpack/bank display, grouping and Chat/HUD notifications can be configured independently. Tracker stock indicators distinguish carried and banked items.
[*]Saved-variable schema 10 upgrades stored profiles before loading, validates imported data and prevents incompatible older builds from changing newer settings. Built-in group overrides and a shared compiled matching cache preserve customization without saving unchanged defaults.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.5.0[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Fixed automatically sized tracker groups reopening after you deliberately closed them. Closed groups now stay closed across inventory changes, settings changes, and UI reloads until you open them again.
[*]Automatic height-related collapses are now temporary and no longer overwrite your saved group preferences. Groups you prefer open can return when space permits.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.4.1[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Groups with more than 200 eligible items now show an overflow message instead of constructing a large list of item rows. Narrow the group's patterns to display its items; summary counts still include all matching items.
[*]Added an amber information icon to oversized groups. Groups with up to 200 eligible items retain their normal item rows and scrolling.
[*]Removed an unwanted debug chat message when the tracking editors reposition the tracker panel.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.4.0[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.3.2[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Refined tracker scrolling so the panel keeps a fixed width, with item names narrowed and counts shifted left only while a scrollbar is visible.
[*]Fixed empty group patterns so they no longer match every item.
[*]Fixed tiny text in group pattern fields and editor search boxes when AddonSelector is not loaded. These fields now use a standard ESO font.
[*]Added Maximum Visible Rows to the Item Tracker Panel settings. The tracker uses single-line names before collapsing categories, and scrolls when the remaining content cannot fit. The title and edit button stay visible.
[*]Opening a category leaves other categories unchanged when they fit; otherwise, the other categories collapse. If all categories fit expanded, the tracker can open them automatically.
[*]Inventory updates that overflow the panel keep the single growing category open if it was already expanded; otherwise, categories collapse. Expansion and collapse choices are remembered.
[*]Added a Tracker Title Size setting with a regular-weight font and a matching edit icon. Item-row text and icons are unchanged.
[*]Added an assignable Show/Hide Item Tracking Panel keybinding and an Open Item Tracking Editor button on the main Inventory Companion addon settings page.
[*]Fixed item names overlapping their counts on the initial tracker render, and made single-line ellipses match item quality colors.
[*]Added a settings button beside the tracker title's edit button to open Inventory Companion's Add-on Settings page directly.
[*]The tracker visibility toggle now hides the panel in inventory, bank, and editor windows too, instead of leaving a visible panel with updates disabled.
[*]Added an Other Settings button beside the title in both tracking editors to return directly to Inventory Companion's Add-on Settings page.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.2.1[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Improved the built-in diagnostic report and performance checks.
[/LIST]

Bank transfers, item tracking, currency notifications, and settings work as before.

[SIZE="2"][B]1.01[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Maintenance update with no changes to everyday features.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.00[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Initial release with crafted-item bank transfers, house-chest stack merging, item and group tracking, and currency and inventory-capacity panels.
[/LIST]
